## 2026-09-04 — Spec 008 T011 Reboot Investigation

- Investigated the owner-reported unexpected reboot around 19:50 EDT using boot history, previous/current kernel journals, sudo/logind records, and SSH service logs.
- At 19:50:15, sudo recorded `dfish` running `/usr/bin/systemctl reboot` from `/home/dfish/dev/ubuntu-media-project`, in login session 4. This proves an explicit software reboot request; these records alone do not identify whether a human or automation issued it.
- The system completed orderly service shutdown and filesystem synchronization at 19:50:19; the next boot began at 19:50:30. SSH started at 19:50:39 and accepted administrator public-key authentication at 19:51:07.
- No kernel panic or abrupt power-loss sequence explains this reboot. Earlier Wi-Fi beacon-loss warnings were present, but the reboot trigger is the recorded sudo command.
- Validation: `journalctl --list-boots`, previous-boot journal and kernel warning review, verbose sudo journal fields, `uptime -s`, and `systemctl is-active ssh` (active). No appliance configuration changed. T011 remains incomplete pending controller/native-input and human-visible Kodi acceptance.

## 2026-09-04 — Spec 008 Native Controller and Media Mode

- Installed the Ubuntu `evtest`, `input-remapper`, `joystick`, and `kodi-peripheral-joystick` packages with an idempotent tracked installer; the in-kernel `hid_playstation` module is available and loaded.
