- Kodi detected the native controller and motion-sensor interfaces. The project owner confirmed joystick control and later confirmed automatic reconnection after timeout by pressing PS once, without re-pairing.
- Added a privacy-safe bounded diagnostic report. It confirms the main controller's 13 buttons, 8 axes, force-feedback capabilities, two joystick interfaces, and Kodi support while intentionally omitting addresses and unique IDs.
- Added an address-free input-remapper preset and explicit `on`, `off`, and `status` wrapper. The mode maps pointer, click, navigation, back, playback, volume, Escape, and Enter primitives and refuses to overwrite local preset modifications.
- Successfully started and stopped injection, confirmed the native device remained available afterward, and kept the mode off for Kodi/future Steam. On the GNOME desktop, the project owner confirmed the controller works well.
- The input-remapper CLI emits a Python 3.14/Pydantic v1 compatibility warning but completed all start/stop operations successfully. Firmware updating remains an optional external action through a PS5 or Sony's Windows application.
- Next task: reboot acceptance, followed by staged downstream checkpoints and final privacy/repository validation.

