## 2026-09-04 — Spec 007 Reboot, Recovery, and Final Acceptance

- Added `scripts/configure-kodi-session.sh` and disabled GNOME idle blanking for the media user at the owner's request; the previous value was 300 seconds and the tracked rollback resets the setting to the Ubuntu default.
- Found that `kodi --standalone` could hang during Quit inside the managed GNOME session. Changed the launcher to `kodi -fs`, which is the appropriate fullscreen mode under the existing window manager.
- Added `TimeoutStopSec=10s` to `media-home.service`. When Kodi hung after an HDMI audio sink failure, the bounded stop terminated the remaining process group and restored GNOME instead of hanging indefinitely.
