- Ran a final watched cycle: local `kodi-send Quit` exited normally with service result `success`, GNOME was visually confirmed, and a subsequent service start visibly restored Kodi. Kodi remains running as the intended appliance state.
- Confirmed the Ubuntu Kodi and `kodi-send` packages are version `2:21.3+dfsg-1ubuntu1`. Shell syntax, systemd unit verification, service/package state, and `git diff --check` passed.
- No Kodi runtime profile files are tracked. Scans found no private keys or likely secret assignments in the feature artifacts.
- NFS remains explicitly out of scope. Spec 007 is complete; DualSense navigation is the next roadmap feature, while receiver/projector/audio acceptance remains deferred in Spec 005.

